.TH ISHTARIA-CLIENT 1 "2026" "ishtaria-client" "Ishtaria"
.SH NAME
ishtaria-client \- client of the Ishtaria virtual planet
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ishtaria-client
[\fB\-\-\fR \fB\-\-server=\fIURL\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Godot 4 client of Ishtaria, a persistent, federated, Earth-sized virtual
planet. Shows an orbiting planet preview, then approaches the server-owned
player location on the surface with a third-person character. The server is
authoritative for game state; the client sends intentions and renders the
acknowledged results.
.PP
On startup the client connects to a world server. The server address is chosen
in this order (highest priority first):
.IP 1. 4
The \fB\-\-server\fR user argument after \fB\-\-\fR, for example
\fBishtaria-client \-\- \-\-server=https://world.example\fR.
.IP 2. 4
The \fBISHTARIA_SERVER_URL\fR environment variable (desktop).
.IP 3. 4
On the browser build, the \fB?server=\fR page parameter, then
\fBwindow.ISHTARIA_SERVER_URL\fR from \fBishtaria-config.js\fR.
.IP 4. 4
The saved address in Godot's \fBuser://client.cfg\fR.
.IP 5. 4
The server the release was built for (\fBhttps://ishtaria.vitexsoftware.com/api\fR in the packages), so that a new
install can be played at once; a client built from source has none and uses the local \fBhttp://127.0.0.1:7400\fR.
.PP
The connection panel accepts a server address at runtime; the last submitted
valid address is saved and restored on startup. Bare addresses such as
\fB127.0.0.1:7400\fR use HTTP; HTTPS, IPv6 and reverse-proxy base paths are
also supported. Remote accounts require HTTPS; plain HTTP is permitted only
for \fBlocalhost\fR, \fB127.0.0.1\fR and \fB::1\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-server= URL
Connect to the given world server URL on startup. Overrides the environment
variable, the saved address and the default. The URL is normalized (a bare
host gets \fBhttp://\fR, a trailing slash is removed); invalid addresses are
ignored and the next source is used. Also accepted as \fB\-\-server\fR
\fIURL\fR (two arguments). Pass after \fB\-\-\fR so the engine does not
interpret it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_SERVER_URL
Default world server URL on desktop. Overridden by the \fB\-\-server\fR
command-line argument.
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_PLAYER_TEST_URL
Test-only server URL for the character creation test. Never point it at a
live game server.
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_TEST_SERVER
World server URL for the world-view screenshot test.
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_ENVIRONMENT_TEST_URL
Optional read-only server URL for the environment test.
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_SLIDE_CAPTURE
Path to a captured server movement trajectory replayed by the controls test.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B user://client.cfg
Saved server address, language, sound and player preferences. Passwords and
session tokens are never written here.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ishtaria-client
Start with the saved or default server (\fBhttp://127.0.0.1:7400\fR).
.TP
.B ishtaria-client \-\- \-\-server=https://world.example
Start connected to a remote world over HTTPS.
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_SERVER_URL=http://192.168.1.10:7400 ishtaria-client
Start connected to a LAN server without changing the saved preference.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ishtaria-admin (1),
.BR ishtaria-server (1)
.PP
The \fBishtaria-client-web\fR package serves the same client as static files
for a browser; the page takes the server from \fB?server=\fR or
\fBishtaria-config.js\fR.
